{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-16T12:58:13.161Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"9d033c4d1e8d3b585e37f1a2","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-16T12:58:13.161Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Behavioural revert proof (real trackers, no SDK mocks): restoring only followCommittedMutations from the base, with its required SDK import, failed both focused regressions (0/2): idle acquired 11 locks versus 5 at the prior observation, and the near-expiry committed CLI fact was absent. Restoring only singleFlightMutationPage to direct SDK delegation failed the two-reader identity assertion (0/1). The initial 100-reader revert diagnostic hit the 30-second test timeout and was terminated; it is not the claimed assertion proof. The smaller two-reader assertion proves the failure directly; the restored test also exercises 100 concurrent identical reads. All functions were restored. Safety regression deliberately aliases the metadata token and advances the safety deadline while using a real skewed CLI commit, requiring an actual SDK read across the prior scan floor."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-16T12:58:13.161Z"}],"before_hash":"902411836106ddb54dd467762ef3d5c5db98df12666505ff7eef91ff8e41c774","after_hash":"e51ffa7c0aa5add2e7a84fa96866ed8aa6539d567e43db13ce4d1c307976ce48","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_cl